Subject: [PATCH] ChFi3d: reconcile the two 2d points of a corner on a CLOSED
 face, not on any periodic one

PerformOneCorner builds two 2d points on the face at the end of the fillet
(pfac1, pfac2) and hands them to ChFi3d_ComputeCurves as Pardeb(3)/Parfin(3).
When that face carries a seam and the corner vertex sits on it, the two points
come off the two different branches of the seam pcurve, and the trim window
built from them (ChFi3d_Boite / ChFi3d_BoundFac, five lines below) then does not
contain the corner vertex.  ChFi3d_Recale exists to bring the pair back onto one
branch, but it was called only in the ChFiDS_OnSame state, and the seam case
arrives here with onsame == False.

Calling it unconditionally (patches/0001-chfi3d-recale-unconditional.patch)
repairs the seam case but breaks two others: blend/simple/H4 and
blend/buildevol/D6 turn from OK into FAILED with an unorientable, non-closed
shell.  The reason is that ChFi3d_Recale tests the periodicity of the BASIS
surface, after the trim has been discarded (ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx:444-447), so on
a face that is periodic but NOT closed its "more than half a period apart" test
is met by two perfectly legal points, and it then shifts one of them a whole
period outside the face.

The missing term is therefore not periodicity but closedness -- "the face trim
spans the whole period", which is exactly what carrying a seam edge means.
BRepAdaptor_Surface::IsUClosed / IsVClosed is OCCT's own test for it
(GeomAdaptor_Surface.cxx:605-616) and needs no new code: Bs is already loaded
from the face with restriction on this path (Bs.Initialize(Fv), :748).

