Both surviving terms (closedness, and the presence of a seam edge) agree on all
three corners.  IsUClosed/IsVClosed is the one taken: O(1), direction-aware, and
already the adaptor's own vocabulary, whereas ChFi3d_Couture builds an edge map
and does not say in which parameter the seam runs.

The `onsame` term is kept first, and short-circuits, so that the OnSame path is
bit-for-bit what it was: there Bs is loaded WITHOUT restriction
(Bs.Initialize(Fv,Standard_False), :698-700) and IsUClosed would not be the
face's own answer but the surface's.

