The one configuration the new term does not separate BY DIRECTION -- a face
closed in U, whose basis is periodic in V as well, but which is not closed in V,
so that ChFi3d_Recale could still shift in V -- probed directly with a torus
whose tube is cut in V and whose revolution is a full turn
(tests-fillet/torus_v_probe.tcl, ptorus 50 10 0 {190,200,270,300} x radius
{1,2,4}, 12 solids, 21 fillets built and 15 refused): the stock log and the
patched log are identical, so the residual is not reached there.  That is a
probe, not a proof; a direction-aware guard would need the test to move inside
ChFi3d_Recale, which has another caller (:4031) and is out of this patch's scope.

